   "note": "The first nine rows give the Holm-adjusted decision for each confirmatory test (H1–H3 × salience, framing, timing; estimates from Tables T3 and T5 and this table; decision = positive coefficient and Holm-adjusted p < .05). H3 models: stake is coded Ukraine 0, Gaza 1, COP 2 and enters linearly with tier (periphery = 1); issue is dropped because stake and issue coincide; random intercepts for outlet nested in country. A positive periphery × stake coefficient means the decline in following from low to high stake is smaller among periphery outlets. The dummy-contrast and V10 models are robustness checks; V10 is the share of an outlet's issue stories whose title names its own country. The second falsifier compares periphery following at high stake (the 8 periphery COP cells; timing 5 with enough events) with the same cells' following against the core series or sample of a different issue (salience: Ukraine core series; framing: Ukraine core sample; timing: core first mentions permuted across events), paired t test, one-sided, Holm-adjusted within the three levels. The within-wars check with a country × issue stake code was not run (see the last row).",
